WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.380
A king in ancient Israel
has abused his power,

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.420
over Bathsheba and her husband, Uriah.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.630
The prophet Nathan faces
him with four words:

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.720
You are the man!

5
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:17.060
In Israel's law, even the king was to
copy God's law and read it all his life.

6
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.400
Can texts this old still guide
leaders, and ethics, today?

7
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.510
In this mission, you'll see how leaders,
from Martin Luther King to the defenders

8
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.320
of apartheid, used the same scriptures.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.120
Then you'll open Genesis and the prophets.

10
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.100
When the Bible pictures
sin as a broken bond,

11
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.960
who is it broken with?

12
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.080
Your mission: find out whether
ancient texts can still guide us,

13
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.190
and what the Bible means by sin.
